 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Totally normal feeling. Lots of people struggle with this. The key is not how often you stop, but that you stop when you need and get back to it feeling refreshed. So, think of it more like a seesaw. You push until you hit a wall, then stop and come back fresh the next day. Honestly, sometimes just getting up and walking around the room is enough. Other times, a quick cup of tea and a few deep breaths can help. Probably for the best. Going through alerts and notifications every couple of hours can break the rhythm and slow you down. Great. And remember, it's okay to take a full lunch break. Going for a walk or having a quick meal with a friend can give you energy back.",
